# Sprint 5
## Production Deployment and Website Integration

Duration:
Sprint 5

---

## Sprint Goal

Deploy DEUS AI into a cloud production environment and integrate it with the BillyMacDeus Blog.

---

## User Stories

### US-011

As a blog reader,

I want to access DEUS AI online,

so that I can ask questions anywhere.

---

### US-012

As a website visitor,

I want DEUS AI embedded into BillyMacDeus Blog,

so that I can interact without leaving the website.

---

### US-013

As a system administrator,

I want automatic knowledge base initialization,

so that deployments require no manual database setup.

---

## Tasks Completed

- Configured Railway deployment
- Configured Cloudflare frontend hosting
- Configured GitHub CI/CD
- Added production CORS configuration
- Added OpenAI environment variables
- Implemented automatic ChromaDB rebuilding
- Connected frontend to Railway backend
- Embedded frontend into Blogger
- Performed production testing

---

## Technical Achievements

### Cloud Deployment

Backend:

- Railway

Frontend:

- Cloudflare

---

### Automatic Database Recovery

The application now detects when the Chroma collection is missing and automatically rebuilds it from embedding JSON files.

This enables clean deployments without committing database artifacts into source control.

---

### Website Integration

DEUS AI was successfully embedded into:

https://blog.billymacdeus.com

using Blogger Pages.

Visitors can interact with DEUS AI directly from the website.

